  "description": "The page-set layer for pure-SSR Fuaran sites. Discovers markdown pages (frontmatter + filename→route derivation), gates the set with a typed SiteCheck (route uniqueness, known-layout membership, non-empty titles, the nav frontmatter contract — an unknown layout is an error, never a silent fall-through), computes a once-at-startup RenderPlan through three host-owned seams (layout dispatch, body renderer, document shell), projects primary navigation from the pages themselves (nav-order/nav-title frontmatter → ordered crawlable Link nodes, current page marked aria-current), and plans the static export (route→file mapping, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, public-asset copy). The host owns content, layout trees, and chrome; this package owns discovery, routes, gates, and export. No Giraffe / ASP.NET / markdown dependency. Apache-2.0 licensed.",
